  "scene": {
    "id": "overlap-pilot3",
    "language": "Okay. So, thinking about the overlap situation in which maybe, you know, I'm the left-back, I'm the left-winger, um, and my teammate has the ball in a position ahead of me, um, with an opponent close to him, I'm sort of gonna run beyond him to try to relieve that- relieve pressure from him, from that opponent, um, so that we can move the team forward. So, I'm gonna un-pause, make a bursting[0] run beyond my teammate. He's going to see me[1] and[2] give me the ball. And at this point, it's all about your proximity, uh, to the ball versus your opponent's proximity to the ball. So, as the ball is coming towards me, I can [3]tell that I'm a lot closer to the ball than my opponent is, and I'm also goal side. Um, and that's the key part here. My opponent's completely blocked off the passing lane to my teammate, but he's left open an entire lane towards goal. So, as soon as I receive the ball, [4]it's just about bursting past- past my opponent, you know, with a quick change of speed. And once I'm close enough to the goal, you know, releasing [5]off a shot into one of the corners to hopefully score a goal.",
